From cf5ba46db4940d2a7d7137c7863feaa941f790ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avi <Avi@yemot.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:12:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Bring IRC servers back up after WeeChat restarts

WeeChat holds no IRC connection across a restart, and nothing brought the
networks back: the add-server flow issued a single /connect and never set
irc.server.<name>.autoconnect. So an unattended library upgrade restarting the
unit was enough to lose every network silently - the relay stayed healthy and
the bot kept answering, with no IRC behind it. One deployment sat like that for
three weeks after a libc6 upgrade restarted WeeChat.

Fix it at both layers. A newly added server gets WeeChat's own autoconnect (and
it is persisted with the /save that already ran), so WeeChat recovers on its
own even when the bridge is not running to see it. On top of that the bridge
sweeps for servers that should be up but are not, every time it attaches to the
relay, which also covers servers added before this change and a network whose
autoconnect attempt failed.

A deliberate disconnect from the menu must survive a restart too, so servers
carry an autoconnect flag (schema 8, existing rows default to on): Disconnect
clears it, Reconnect and a re-add set it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
